[0;37m  [1;32mCONFIG[0;37m on its own lists the pages. [1;32mCONFIG[0;37m and a page name opens one:
[0;37m  [1;32mCONFIG board[0;37m is the first. [1;32mF1[0;37m saves a page and most changes apply at once.

[1;36m  THE PAGES
[1;32m  board     [0;37mthe board's name, its hostname on the network, the timezone
[0;37m            and NTP server, idle minutes, the LED pin, where callers land
[1;32m  limits    [0;37mminutes per call and per day, the WHO refresh, the account cap
[1;32m  accounts  [0;37mwhether callers may sign up, whether guests may call, and for
[0;37m            how many minutes
[1;32m  backup    [0;37mthe port, how long the window stays open, the button pin
[1;32m  staff     [0;37mthe passwords you just set
[1;32m  wifi      [0;37mthe network; a change is used from the next restart

[0;37m  And one page for each plugin: [1;32mchat[0;37m, [1;32mforums[0;37m, [1;32mfiles[0;37m, [1;32minfo[0;37m, [1;32mannounce
[0;37m  and [1;32msd[0;37m. Each starts with whether it is on and who may use it.

